  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Elephant conservation &amp; capacity building in Seima Protection Forest, Cambodia - Year 8</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to sustain and improve conservation of Asian elephants and build capacity of rangers and community patrols in Seima Protection Forest. Project activities will include: 1) implement anti-poaching patrols and monitoring of elephant habitat; 2) monitor forest loss and encroachment using remote sensing and Geographic Information Systems; 3) establish community patrol teams in one new village; 4) increase capacity of new and existing community patrols through training and equipment; 5) establish a reporting network for human-elephant conflict; 6) conduct extensive training for field teams on survey methods and protocols; and 7) conduct the HEC survey in parallel with the elephant DNA survey. This project will contribute to a well-managed forest landscape that supports increasing wildlife populations and improved livelihoods for the communities of the Seima Protection Forest.</narrative>
  </description>
